ite the error prompt, the printer continues to print normally. The issue may be related to a faulty or misaligned paper sensor.\r\nAction Taken: Inspected and cleaned the paper feed area and rollers; reloaded paper and reset the printer. Printing functionality verified, but the E02 error still appears intermittently.\r\nRecommendation: Monitor printer behavior; if the error persists, consider checking or replacing the paper sensor to fully resolve the issue.','10.40.0.10','2025-10-10 06:39:13','2025-10-10 08:39:58'),(1286,404,1,1,'Completed','Cant access wifi','The network password has been reset. Please use the following format to log in:\r\nFirst three letters of your middle name (Capitalized) followed by your birthday in this format — DD.MM.YYYY.\r\nExample: DEL23.04.1998','10.40.0.10','2025-10-10 07:41:11','2025-10-13 00:13:52'),(1287,127,4,3,'Completed','IRO telephone keeps displaying incorrect date & time. Unable to set manually.',NULL,'10.40.0.10','2025-10-10 08:10:07','2025-10-16 01:29:56'),(1288,127,4,3,'Completed','IRO telephone keeps displaying incorrect date & time. Unable to set manually.',NULL,'10.40.0.10','2025-10-10 08:10:09','2025-10-16 01:30:06'),(1289,419,1,1,'Completed','Cant access wifi','The network password has been reset. Please use the following format to log in:\r\nFirst three letters of your middle name (with Capitalized) followed by your birthday in this format — DD.MM.YYYY.\r\nExample: DEL23.04.1998','10.40.0.10','2025-10-11 12:56:46','2025-10-13 00:13:14'),(1290,77,4,1,'Completed',NULL,'Wi-Fi disconnected. Relogin','10.40.0.10','2025-10-13 00:46:50','2025-10-14 05:22:45'),(1291,111,1,2,'Completed',NULL,'Issue:PC not turning on but power is detected.\r\nFindings:Power indicator was active, but the system did not boot. Issue traced to loose RAM or power connection.\r\nAction Taken:Reseated the RAM module and reconnected power cables. After reseating, the PC powered on successfully and booted normally.\r\nRecommendation:Ensure all internal